[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Play Skyrim Together Reborn with your friends — on Windows or Linux — in one click. No Vortex, no Mod Organizer 2, no manual file shuffling: STR Launcher finds your Skyrim install, downloads and installs the mod for you, checks that everything is ready, and gets you straight into a multiplayer session. One self-contained program, no installer, no runtime dependencies — and every change it makes can be undone with a single click.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1][*]Download STR Launcher from the Files tab and run it. It finds your Skyrim install automatically.
[*]Open Settings → Nexus Mods and paste your Nexus API key (generate one in your Nexus account settings → Personal API keys). One-time only; the key is stored on your PC.
[*]Press [b]Install Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] and wait for the readiness checklist to go green. It verifies your game version, Address Library, plugins and (on Linux) Proton, so nothing fails silently.
[*]Press [b]Launch Together[/b]. In-game, press [b]F2[/b] to open the multiplayer menu, create a party, and invite your friends.
[/list]
[b]No API key? Offline mode:[/b] download the two archives manually — [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993?tab=files]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444?tab=files]Address Library[/url] — drop them in under Settings → Offline mode, and press Install.
[list=1][*]Finish the Helgen intro [b]before[/b] connecting to a server — see the official [url=https://wiki.tiltedphoques.com/tilted-online/general-information/playguide]play guide[/url] (one minute, well worth it).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list][*][b]One-click install[/b] — auto-detects your Skyrim, downloads Skyrim Together Reborn and Address Library through the Nexus API, and installs them.
[*][b]Readiness checklist[/b] — checks game version, Address Library, plugins and Proton before every launch, so nothing fails silently.
[*][b]Launch Together[/b] — starts the modded game straight from the launcher. On Linux it pins GE-Proton 10 automatically (GE-Proton 11 crashes Skyrim Together 1.8) and can either replace the Skyrim launcher or add a separate "Skyrim Together Reborn" entry to your Steam library with its own artwork.
[*][b]Full undo[/b] — removed Creation Club content goes to a backup folder, a manifest records every file the launcher touched, and Undo restores your Skyrim to exactly how it was.
[*][b]Offline mode[/b] — no Nexus API key needed; point it at the two archives you downloaded yourself.
[*][b]Steam Deck friendly[/b] — works on Linux and the Deck out of the box, no custom launch options required.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list][*]Skyrim Special Edition (Steam, v1.6 or newer), launched once through Steam first — reach the main menu, then quit. The Anniversary Upgrade DLC is not needed and is best disabled.
[*]A free Nexus Mods account (for the automatic downloads).
[*]Windows 8.1 or newer, or Linux (Steam Deck works great).
[*]All players on the same Skyrim Together version, and no other mods — extra mods are the #1 cause of crashes with Skyrim Together.
[*]GOG/Epic copies: automatic Steam detection and launch integrations are Steam-only, but the installer still works — point it at your SkyrimSE.exe under Settings → Game → Browse.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Shout outs[/b][/size]
[list][*][url=https://github.com/tiltedphoques]Tilted Phoques[/url] — Skyrim Together Reborn itself, and the dragon emblem used in this launcher's icon.
[*][url=https://github.com/Cyphs/SteamDeckSTR]Cyphs[/url] (building on [url=https://github.com/pikdum/steam-deck]pikdum[/url]'s scripts) — the Linux approach (launcher replacement, protonfixes localfix, config.vdf handling) is ported from their MIT-licensed work.
[*][url=https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom]GloriousEggroll[/url] — GE-Proton.
[*][url=https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Cinzel]Cinzel[/url] (SIL Open Font License) — the carved-caps Skyrim-style heading font bundled with the launcher.
[/list]
